{
	"nodes":[
		{"id":"a000000000000001","type":"file","file":"Sectors/Semiconductor Capital Equipment.md","x":-700,"y":-1280,"width":700,"height":320,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"a000000000000002","type":"text","x":60,"y":-1280,"width":820,"height":320,"color":"5","text":"## AI Infrastructure Full Stack\n\n**Materials → Equipment → Foundries/Memory → AI Chips → Power/Networking/Storage → Hyperscalers → Software Workloads**\n\nHyperscaler CY26 capex floor: **$600–750B (+36% YoY, ~75% AI-directed)** — unprecedented multi-year visibility. Each layer's pricing power depends on which oligopolies remain intact: ASML (EUV 100%), TSMC (advanced foundry >90%), NVDA (training ~85%), SK Hynix+Samsung+Micron (HBM triopoly), AWS+Azure+GCP+Oracle (hyperscale cloud).\n\n**Cycle has shifted from capacity → complexity**. Dominant risk vectors: inference-efficiency shock (DeepSeek-style), Taiwan tail, hyperscaler capex deceleration below the $600B floor, MATCH Act servicing controls.\n\nCY26 anchors: WFE $135B · TSMC capex $52–56B · Hyperscaler capex $600–750B · NVDA Blackwell + Rubin ramp · 18A HVM Q1"},
		{"id":"b100000000000001","type":"group","x":-2500,"y":-880,"width":640,"height":1620,"label":"Upstream Inputs & Substrates","color":"4"},
		{"id":"a000000000000010","type":"text","x":-2460,"y":-820,"width":560,"height":140,"text":"**Photoresists & Photomasks**\n\nJSR · TOK · Shin-Etsu Chemical · Hoya · Photronics — EUV resist bottleneck"},
		{"id":"a000000000000011","type":"text","x":-2460,"y":-660,"width":560,"height":140,"text":"**Process Gases & Specialty Chemicals**\n\nLinde · Air Liquide · Air Products · Entegris · Versum — single-supplier exposure on exotic precursors"},
		{"id":"a000000000000012","type":"text","x":-2460,"y":-500,"width":560,"height":140,"text":"**Silicon Wafers (Si)**\n\nShin-Etsu · SUMCO · Siltronic · GlobalWafers — top-4 ≈ 90%; 300mm capacity tight"},
		{"id":"a000000000000013","type":"file","file":"Theses/IQE - IQE.md","x":-2460,"y":-340,"width":560,"height":220,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"a000000000000014","type":"file","file":"Theses/2802 - Ajinomoto.md","x":-2460,"y":-100,"width":560,"height":220,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"a000000000000015","type":"text","x":-2460,"y":140,"width":560,"height":140,"text":"**Carl Zeiss SMT — EUV optics**\n\nLocked-in optics partner to ASML; sole High-NA mirror supplier; 24.9% ASML equity stake since 2016"},
		{"id":"a000000000000016","type":"text","x":-2460,"y":300,"width":560,"height":140,"text":"**ABF Substrate Supply Chain**\n\nUnimicron · Nan Ya PCB · Ibiden · Shinko · Kinsus — ABF substrates for FCBGA/CoWoS; see [[Sectors/ABF Substrates & Advanced Packaging Supply Chain]]"},
		{"id":"a000000000000017","type":"text","x":-2460,"y":460,"width":560,"height":240,"text":"**Lasertec — EUV Mask Inspection**\n\nACTIS platform ~95% share; sole actinic-pattern mask inspection vendor. Customer base: TSMC, Intel, Samsung, ASML R&D, imec. ZEISS now competing on High-NA mask metrology."},
		{"id":"b100000000000002","type":"group","x":-1830,"y":-880,"width":1700,"height":560,"label":"WFE — Lithography & Patterning (~$28B CY26E)","color":"5"},
		{"id":"a000000000000020","type":"text","x":-1790,"y":-820,"width":540,"height":480,"text":"## ASML\n\n**EUV monopoly — 100% share**\n\n- NXE:3800 (Low-NA) shipping volume\n- EXE:5200B (High-NA) — >€400M ASP\n- ~12 High-NA units placed by Apr 2026 (Intel, Samsung, SK Hynix, imec, TSMC R&D)\n- DUV: ~94% lithography share\n- 2012 customer co-invest (Intel €829M, TSMC, Samsung)\n- China exposure guided down to ~20% of 2026 sales (was 33% 2025)\n\n**Catalysts**: 5–10 High-NA in 2026; MATCH Act DUV/servicing controls; TSMC 1.4nm High-NA decision"},
		{"id":"a000000000000021","type":"text","x":-1230,"y":-820,"width":540,"height":220,"text":"**Nikon · Canon — Legacy DUV**\n\ni-line and KrF dominance; lost ArF immersion to ASML by mid-2000s. Defensive moat in older nodes (mature analog/power). Negligible at advanced logic."},
		{"id":"a000000000000022","type":"text","x":-1230,"y":-580,"width":540,"height":220,"text":"**Tokyo Electron (TEL) — Coater/Developer ~92%**\n\nMonopoly in track tools that pair with every EUV/DUV scanner; cryogenic etch in HVM 2026 for 400L NAND. Also strong in CVD, etch, batch processing."},
		{"id":"a000000000000023","type":"text","x":-670,"y":-820,"width":480,"height":460,"text":"## Sub-Function ASPs\n\n**Per-tool inflation last decade**:\n- EUV: $120M → $200M → **>€400M** (3.3x)\n- BESI HB: +20% Gen-1 → Gen-2\n- AMAT Sym3 etch: ~2x across FinFET → GAA\n\n**Service annuity** (45K+ AMAT tools, 100K+ LRCX chambers): stable double-digit growth regardless of capex cycle. KLAC service raised to 13–15% CAGR, $6B target by 2030.\n\n**Pricing power = consolidation × node complexity × installed-base lock-in**"},
		{"id":"b100000000000003","type":"group","x":-1830,"y":-300,"width":1700,"height":920,"label":"WFE — Deposition / Etch (~$58B CY26E TAM)","color":"5"},
		{"id":"a000000000000030","type":"file","file":"Theses/AMAT - Applied Materials.md","x":-1790,"y":-240,"width":540,"height":280,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"a000000000000031","type":"file","file":"Theses/LRCX - Lam Research.md","x":-1230,"y":-240,"width":540,"height":280,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"a000000000000032","type":"file","file":"Theses/ASMI - ASM International.md","x":-670,"y":-240,"width":480,"height":280,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"a000000000000033","type":"text","x":-1790,"y":60,"width":540,"height":260,"text":"**Tokyo Electron (TEL) — Etch & Furnace**\n\nDominant in coater/developer (~92%); also etch, batch CVD, single-wafer epi. Cryogenic etch HVM 2026 for 400L NAND. Customer base anchored in Kioxia/Samsung memory + TSMC."},
		{"id":"a000000000000034","type":"text","x":-1230,"y":60,"width":540,"height":260,"text":"**Kokusai Electric (Hitachi-affiliated)**\n\nBatch ALD ~70% share — the underappreciated GAA beneficiary. ASMI rival in single-wafer; Kokusai dominant in batch furnaces. Hitachi spun out 2017; listed 2023."},
		{"id":"a000000000000035","type":"file","file":"Theses/AIXA - Aixtron.md","x":-670,"y":60,"width":480,"height":260,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"a000000000000036","type":"text","x":-1790,"y":340,"width":1090,"height":240,"text":"## Function Coverage Matrix\n\n| Function | Leader | Share | Secondary |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| CVD (PECVD/SACVD) | AMAT | ~30% | LRCX, TEL, Kokusai |\n| PVD | AMAT | ~70% | ULVAC |\n| ALD (single-wafer) | ASMI | ~55% | AMAT, LRCX |\n| ALD (batch) | Kokusai | ~70% | TEL, ASMI |\n| Etch (conductor + dielectric) | LRCX | ~50% | TEL, AMAT |\n| Epi (Si) | AMAT | ~55% | ASMI |\n| MOCVD (compound semi) | Aixtron | ~50% | Veeco |\n| CMP | AMAT | ~70% | Ebara |\n| Ion implant | AMAT | ~70% | Axcelis (merging w/ Veeco H2 2026) |"},
		{"id":"a000000000000037","type":"text","x":-670,"y":340,"width":480,"height":240,"text":"**GAA inflection — tripling of ALD/selective-etch SAM**\n\n- ASMI: 12%+ CAGR through 2030 on GAA\n- LRCX: GAA rev triples CY2026; Akara etch + Aether dry resist + ALTUS Halo\n- AMAT: >20% CY26 equipment growth guide\n- TSM N2 HVM Q4 2025; Samsung SF2P 70% yield Jan 26; Intel 18A HVM Jan 26"},
		{"id":"b100000000000004","type":"group","x":-1830,"y":640,"width":1700,"height":380,"label":"WFE — Process Control / Metrology / Inspection (~$13B)","color":"5"},
		{"id":"a000000000000040","type":"file","file":"Theses/KLA - KLA Corporation.md","x":-1790,"y":700,"width":700,"height":300,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"a000000000000041","type":"text","x":-1070,"y":700,"width":540,"height":300,"text":"**Lasertec · Onto · Camtek · ZEISS**\n\n- Lasertec ACTIS — ~95% EUV mask inspection\n- Onto Innovation — advanced metrology, HBM bumps\n- Camtek — 2D/3D back-end metrology\n- ZEISS SMT — High-NA mask metrology entry"},
		{"id":"a000000000000042","type":"text","x":-510,"y":700,"width":380,"height":300,"text":"**Intensity rising 100–200bp/node**\n\nProcess control share of WFE expanding from ~10% to 15%+ as defect-density tolerance shrinks at GAA + EUV + hybrid bonding intersections. KLAC 73% ROIC — sector-best. 3x inspection intensity in adv packaging."},
		{"id":"b100000000000005","type":"group","x":-1830,"y":1040,"width":1700,"height":380,"label":"WFE — Test & Probe (~$8–9B)","color":"5"},
		{"id":"a000000000000050","type":"file","file":"Theses/FORM - FormFactor.md","x":-1790,"y":1100,"width":540,"height":300,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"a000000000000051","type":"file","file":"Theses/AEHR - Aehr Test Systems.md","x":-1230,"y":1100,"width":540,"height":300,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"a000000000000052","type":"text","x":-670,"y":1100,"width":480,"height":300,"text":"**Teradyne · Advantest — ATE**\n\n- Advantest — memory-dominant; primary HBM4 tester; AI accelerator (NVDA, AMD)\n- Teradyne — SoC + memory; auto/industrial recovery\n\nCombined ATE ~$5–6B; HBM test intensity 2–3x DRAM baseline."},
		{"id":"b100000000000006","type":"group","x":-1830,"y":1440,"width":1700,"height":380,"label":"WFE — Advanced Packaging & 3D Integration (~$12B → 15–20% of WFE by 2028)","color":"5"},
		{"id":"a000000000000060","type":"file","file":"Theses/BESI - BE Semiconductor Industries.md","x":-1790,"y":1500,"width":540,"height":300,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"a000000000000061","type":"text","x":-1230,"y":1500,"width":540,"height":300,"text":"**Kinex (AMAT + BESI integrated D2W)**\n\nFirst mass-prod order Mar 2026 from SK Hynix — **logic/DRAM, not HBM** (HBM5 deferred to 2028-29 per JEDEC 900µm relaxation). 30 bonders deployed at one customer."},
		{"id":"a000000000000062","type":"text","x":-670,"y":1500,"width":480,"height":300,"text":"**ASMPT · Disco · Hanmi**\n\n- ASMPT — wirebond + flip-chip\n- Disco — wafer dicing/grinding monopoly\n- Hanmi — TC bonders for HBM stacking\n\nCoWoS scaling 75–80K → 120–130K wfm by late 2026 (3.7x since 2024)."},
		{"id":"b100000000000007","type":"group","x":-1830,"y":1840,"width":1700,"height":380,"label":"Chinese Domestic Equipment — 35% China share 2025 (target 50–60% by 2030)","color":"2"},
		{"id":"a000000000000070","type":"text","x":-1790,"y":1900,"width":540,"height":300,"text":"**NAURA — Etch + CVD**\n\nFY2025 rev CNY 39.35B (~$5.4B, +30.85% YoY). Only Chinese vendor at Tier-2-Western scale. Etch + thin-film deposition already >40% domestic share."},
		{"id":"a000000000000071","type":"text","x":-1230,"y":1900,"width":540,"height":300,"text":"**AMEC — Etch**\n\n5nm etch validating at TSMC; not yet HVM. Most likely Chinese vendor to break into advanced logic-grade etch first."},
		{"id":"a000000000000072","type":"text","x":-670,"y":1900,"width":480,"height":300,"text":"**Piotech · ACM · SiCarrier**\n\n- Piotech — ALD/CVD\n- ACM Research — cleaning, ECP\n- SiCarrier — full-stack equipment integrator (Huawei-backed)\n\nZero Chinese capability in EUV, process control, hybrid bonding."},
		{"id":"b100000000000008","type":"group","x":180,"y":-880,"width":920,"height":1140,"label":"Customers — Leading-Edge Foundries & IDMs","color":"2"},
		{"id":"a000000000000080","type":"file","file":"Theses/TSM - Taiwan Semiconductor.md","x":220,"y":-820,"width":440,"height":300,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"a000000000000081","type":"file","file":"Theses/INTC - Intel.md","x":680,"y":-820,"width":400,"height":300,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"a000000000000082","type":"text","x":220,"y":-500,"width":440,"height":220,"text":"**Samsung Foundry**\n\nSF2P qualified 70% yield Jan 2026 (from 30%); first EXE:5200B High-NA late 2025; second unit H1 2026 (Taylor, TX). Aggressive pricing to recapture share."},
		{"id":"a000000000000083","type":"text","x":680,"y":-500,"width":400,"height":220,"text":"**GlobalFoundries · UMC · SMIC**\n\nMature node (28nm+): GFS, UMC. SMIC = China leading-edge attempt, 7nm via DUV multi-patterning. Volume but not advanced-equipment customer."},
		{"id":"a000000000000084","type":"file","file":"Sectors/Semiconductor Foundries.md","x":220,"y":-260,"width":860,"height":240,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"a000000000000085","type":"text","x":220,"y":0,"width":860,"height":240,"text":"## Foundry Capex CY26\n\n- **TSMC**: $52–56B (+27–40% vs $40.9B 2025) — 10–20% to AP\n- **Intel**: 18A HVM Jan 2026 (Fab 52); world's first commercial High-NA line at 30K wpw\n- **Samsung Foundry**: ~$25–30B; SF2P ramp\n- **CoWoS bottleneck**: 75–80K → 120–130K wfm by late 2026; outsourcing 240–270K wafers annually to Amkor/SPIL"},
		{"id":"b100000000000009","type":"group","x":180,"y":280,"width":920,"height":1140,"label":"Customers — Memory IDMs","color":"2"},
		{"id":"a000000000000090","type":"file","file":"Theses/000660 - SK Hynix.md","x":220,"y":340,"width":440,"height":300,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"a000000000000091","type":"file","file":"Theses/285A - Kioxia.md","x":680,"y":340,"width":400,"height":300,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"a000000000000092","type":"file","file":"Theses/SNDK - SanDisk.md","x":220,"y":660,"width":440,"height":280,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"a000000000000093","type":"text","x":680,"y":660,"width":400,"height":280,"text":"**Micron · Samsung Memory**\n\n- Micron capex $13.5B (+23%) — DRAM/NAND/HBM3E ramp\n- Samsung Memory capex $20B (+11%)\n- SK Hynix capex $20.5B (+17%)\n\nHBM4 16-Hi on microbump (not HB) — JEDEC 900µm relaxation Apr 2026."},
		{"id":"a000000000000094","type":"file","file":"Sectors/DRAM & HBM Memory.md","x":220,"y":960,"width":860,"height":220,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"a000000000000095","type":"file","file":"Sectors/NAND Memory & Storage.md","x":220,"y":1200,"width":860,"height":200,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"b100000000000010","type":"group","x":1180,"y":-880,"width":920,"height":1140,"label":"End Markets — AI Compute & Demand Drivers","color":"1"},
		{"id":"a0000000000000a0","type":"file","file":"Theses/NVDA - Nvidia.md","x":1220,"y":-820,"width":440,"height":280,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"a0000000000000a1","type":"file","file":"Theses/AMD - Advanced Micro Devices.md","x":1680,"y":-820,"width":400,"height":280,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"a0000000000000a2","type":"file","file":"Theses/AVGO - Broadcom.md","x":1220,"y":-520,"width":440,"height":280,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"a0000000000000a3","type":"file","file":"Theses/MRVL - Marvell Technology.md","x":1680,"y":-520,"width":400,"height":280,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"a0000000000000a4","type":"file","file":"Theses/CRWV - CoreWeave.md","x":1220,"y":-220,"width":440,"height":260,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"a0000000000000a5","type":"text","x":1680,"y":-220,"width":400,"height":260,"text":"**Hyperscaler Capex CY26 ~$600–750B (+36% YoY)**\n\nAmazon $200B · Google $175–185B · Meta $115–135B · Microsoft $120B+ · Oracle $50B\n\n~75% AI-directed. Floor underpins WFE through CY28 absent inference-efficiency shock (DeepSeek-style)."},
		{"id":"a0000000000000a6","type":"text","x":1220,"y":60,"width":860,"height":180,"text":"**NVDA = 60%+ TSMC CoWoS bookings 2026–27** — single-customer concentration is the source of equipment-cycle correlation to AI. AMD/AVGO/MRVL = the diversification tail."},
		{"id":"b100000000000011","type":"group","x":1180,"y":280,"width":920,"height":320,"label":"End Markets — Photonics & Optical Networking","color":"1"},
		{"id":"a0000000000000b0","type":"file","file":"Theses/LITE - Lumentum.md","x":1220,"y":340,"width":440,"height":220,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"a0000000000000b1","type":"text","x":1680,"y":340,"width":400,"height":220,"text":"**SiPh / CPO transition**\n\nDrives demand for AIXA G10-AsP MOCVD, IQE III-V epi, FORM optical probes, AEHR photonics WLBI."},
		{"id":"b100000000000012","type":"group","x":1180,"y":620,"width":920,"height":320,"label":"Adjacent — Data Center Power & Cooling","color":"1"},
